<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25259" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jŏvĭus</span></b> , ii,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a surname of the emperor
			Diocletian</i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jŏ-vĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Diocletian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cohors,</span>”
				<i>a legion of honor instituted by Diocletian</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. B. Gild. 418</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jŏ-vĭānus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., the same; hence, <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Jŏvĭāni</span></b> , <i>soldiers of Diocletian's legion of honor</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Amm. 22, 3, 2 al.</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
